From 42b60458b25e4775cce78d87060b4e605e687c75 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 04:44:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Keep the student websites' name for student websites only

fullstack-student.heraldcollege.edu.np answered for everything the
server serves: the sign-up page, phpMyAdmin and, on port 8443, the admin
panel's sign-in page, which a tester found and took for a second portal.
It now serves students' websites and nothing else (any other path is a
404), and port 8443 refuses the connection for that name.

fullstack.heraldcollege.edu.np, and the bare IP, keep sign-up,
phpMyAdmin and the admin panel, and send any student page asked for
there to the student name. Students' pages run their own scripts, so
they no longer share an address, and with it cookies, with phpMyAdmin
or the sign-up page.

The health check asks for student pages on their own name and checks
that the two are kept apart. The README says which name serves what,
the panel's empty student list no longer points people to the student
name to sign up, and the student guide suggests the IP only for logins
and uploads.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013bR1gBZC9XYizdKhzmoXVF
